--!strict
--[[
	Quests - every quest and questline (vault: 03-Content/Quests). The server engine is
	ServerScriptService/Progression/QuestService.

	Lines
	  Prologue   "What the Barges Bring": arrive, survive, salvage, sort, check in with your
	             side (picked on the intro screen before the first spawn).
	  Menders   "Clean Slate": sort, purify and protect, up to M1 Mastery (C1-C11), then
	             Act III "Clear Skies" (C12-C16, levels 24-32): the outer biomes, Apex
	             Smoglings, a Turf War, Keeper Sable at the Smog Spire, and clearing the air.
	  Scrappers    "Take What's Left": strip, sell and smelt, up to M1 Mastery (R1-R11), then
	             Act III "Rule the Heap" (R12-R16): the same road, ending in bounties and alloy.
	  Side       townsfolk of the Gate Market and the outer biomes (Sable, Fern, Hale); each
	             teaches a real-world Field Note.
	  Job        repeatable work: Clerk Odo's board, and the quartermasters' trophy runs.
	Both faction lines share a shape (talk, salvage, upgrade, Smoglings, a faction process, a Sky
	Dump, the Wastezone, the Junk Ram, then the outer biomes, the apex beasts, the hill and the
	tower) so neither side is the easy one; what differs is HOW they treat the trash, and the
	Field Notes they unlock.

	Steps run in order. Step types and their `target`:
	  Talk      npc id, or "Recruiter" (your own faction's recruiter)
	  Visit     region key (MapRegionVolumes)
	  Salvage   region key or nil      Recycle   nil (items sorted at a Recycling Station)
	  Sell      nil (items sold)       Craft     recipe id
	  Process   recipe id (Purify / Smelt)       Collect   item id (have `count`)
	  Deliver   item id (handed to the turn-in NPC, consumed)
	  Consume   "Food" | "Water" | item id      Defeat    "Smogling" | "JunkRam" | "Rival"
	  Upgrade   nil (Relic at tier >= count)    Contest   nil (salvage during an open Sky Dump)
	  Faction   nil (join a faction)            Roll      nil (roll a Relic)
	  Smash     nil (parts of the map you broke, counted per part)
	  Air       "Clear" (the server's air is Clear Skies while the step is open)
	  Turf      nil (your side wins a Turf War while you take part)
	  Bounty    nil (claim the bounty on a Wanted rival)
	  Notes     nil (have `count` Field Notes)
	  Defeat also takes "ApexSmogling" (which also counts as a "Smogling")
	Rewards may carry a `title` (Shared/Data/Titles).
	Rewards are PROPOSALS (2026-10-25).
]]

export type Step = { text: string, type: string, target: string?, count: number? }
export type Rewards = {
	title: string?, -- a title id (Shared/Data/Titles) to wear over your head
	exp: number?,
	dollars: number?,
	scrap: number?,
	residue: number?,
	standing: number?,
	items: { [string]: number }?,
}
export type Quest = {
	id: string,
	title: string,
	line: string,
	kind: string, -- Main | Side | Job
	giver: string,
	turnIn: string?, -- defaults to the giver
	auto: boolean?, -- completes on its last step without a turn-in
	autoStart: boolean?, -- given to every new character
	faction: string?, -- Menders | Scrappers | Unaligned (only then)
	requires: { level: number?, quests: { string }?, faction: boolean? }?,
	repeatable: number?, -- seconds before it can be taken again
	summary: string,
	steps: { Step },
	rewards: Rewards,
	note: string?,
	offer: { string },
	progress: { string }?,
	complete: { string },
}

